      "text": "PART 4\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        622.11474609375,
        516.8572998046875,
        760.0736083984375
      ],
      "text": "It’s only relatively recently that designers have become aware of the need to\nbe inclusive when designing products. But what does that mean exactly? Well,\nit simply means designing products that span economic, social and cultural\nbarriers. It means making sure products are accessible, so that as many\ndifferent types of ...people as possible can use them, without any type of\nadaptation having to be made to the original design. Inclusive design is often\nlinked with universal design, although they are not quite the same thing.\n"
    }
